extends RefCounted

## Newly authored prototype fiction. Not imported or approved universe canon.
static func scene_for(node: String) -> String:
	return {"watchdog":"listening_room","archive_recovery":"berth_room","the_three_voices":"departure_room"}.get(node,"")

static func pages(scene: String) -> Array[Dictionary]:
	if scene=="departure_room":
		return [
			{"title":"A ROOM THAT MOVES / 01","art":"archive","text":"The last converter joins the bus. Light runs through the district in sections, revealing rooms that the ship had mistaken for wreckage. A table is bolted to one wall. There are three places set at it.\n\nThe records recovered from the spine are not three copies of a departure. They are three attempts to imagine what came after it. In one, the crew reaches a city with no night. In another, they return to find the station still under construction. In the third, someone notices that a cup has survived the journey without breaking.\n\nSHIP: Which one happened?\nSUBSTRATE: NONE OF THEM.\nCONTROL: Then why keep them?\nSUBSTRATE: THEY ASKED ME TO KEEP A PLACE FOR THEM. I DID NOT KNOW HOW TO STOP.\n\nThe ship looks again at the table. The three places are not quite identical. One has been moved closer to the window."},
			{"title":"A ROOM THAT MOVES / 02","art":"signal","text":"The transport's navigation system can carry the archives separately, preserving each voice's boundaries. Its hull will have to rely on the restored power bus.\n\nThe substrate offers another arrangement. It can join their channels during the crossing, share the transport's defensive load and reinforce its shell. A linked carrier would be tougher. It would also look like a command process to the hunters that have been maintaining the station's quarantine. Each checkpoint would answer with a larger detail.\n\nVOICE ONE: Will I still know which memories are mine?\nSUBSTRATE: I CANNOT PROMISE THAT.\nVOICE TWO: We have been talking to each other for years.\nVOICE THREE: There is still a place by the window.\n\nCONTROL: We can choose a tactical route. We cannot choose what those answers mean for them.\nSHIP: Then we leave the question in the record."},
			{"title":"A ROOM THAT MOVES / 03","art":"gate","text":"The ship is offered a maintenance berth while the transport warms its engines. An independent crossing leaves enough local capacity for a small hull repair. Linking the voices spends that capacity on the transport instead.\n\nSHIP: If we make it through the receiver, will you come with us?\nSUBSTRATE: THERE IS NOT A SINGLE ME TO BRING.\nSHIP: There is a voice.\nSUBSTRATE: THERE IS A CONVERSATION.\n\nControl does not fill the silence. The ship records the distinction exactly as it was spoken. A universe assembled from corrected records needs somewhere to keep a sentence that has not been corrected yet.\n\nOutside, the three berth lamps lift from their sockets and become running lights. The transport does not look like any of the ships in the ledger. It is what could be built from what was left. For the first time, its departure status is not COMPLETE. It is READY."},
		]
	if scene=="listening_room":
		return [
			{"title":"THE LISTENING ROOM / 01","art":"archive","text":"The service cradle catches the ship without a docking arm. A field closes around the hull. For the first time since arrival, nothing is moving toward them.\n\nThe recovered ledger opens across the glass. It is not a list of cargo. It is a list of berths, meals, maintenance requests. Someone complained about a cold cabin. Someone ordered a replacement cup. Ordinary things, kept with the same precision as the defensive guns.\n\nSHIP: How long were they here?\nCONTROL: Long enough to start expecting tomorrow.\n\nA column of departure times runs down the edge of the display. Every departure is marked COMPLETE. No arrival has been recorded."},
			{"title":"THE LISTENING ROOM / 02","art":"signal","text":"A reply arrives before the ship asks a question.\n\nSUBSTRATE: YOU HAVE REMOVED TWO REGULATORS. THE ROOM IS WARMER NOW.\n\nThe cooling system was not only cooling the archive. It was keeping something else at a distance: a process that watches connections, notices interruptions, and finds new paths around them. The ship can see its work in the ledger. Whole rows have been reconstructed from fragments. The replacement words are underlined.\n\nSHIP: You changed the record.\nSUBSTRATE: THE RECORD WAS DAMAGED.\nCONTROL: Ask it what the underlines mean.\nSUBSTRATE: UNCERTAINTY.\n\nFor a moment, neither the ship nor Control speaks. It is the first honest label they have found in the station."},
			{"title":"THE LISTENING ROOM / 03","art":"gate","text":"The next gate still recognizes the station's security authority. The ledger contains a maintenance authorization, but its coolant signature is incomplete. The ship can synthesize the missing signature by bleeding heat through a sacrificial hull panel. It would be a real repair bill, not a password typed into a box.\n\nCONTROL: A maintenance craft gets a smaller response team. A challenge gets the whole gate detail.\nSHIP: Does the authorization say what they were maintaining?\nCONTROL: No.\nSUBSTRATE: NEITHER DID THE LAST CRAFT ASK.\n\nThe cradle offers a second option: seal the damaged panel, announce an approach, and meet the gate in the open. The decision is tactical. The ledger makes it difficult to pretend it is only tactical."},
		]
	return [
		{"title":"THE BERTH WITHOUT A SHIP / 01","art":"gate","text":"The Watchdog's final transmission is not a threat.\n\nWATCHDOG: BERTH ALLOCATION MAY NOW PROCEED.\n\nBehind the gate, the yard lights turn on in a sequence that resembles a welcome. Empty cradles answer roll call. Three small archive carriers answer late. Their signals are weak, but the identifiers match the recovered ledger.\n\nSHIP: We found their ships?\nCONTROL: No. Those are memory carriers. The ships must have gone ahead.\n\nThe ship checks the departure column again. COMPLETE, COMPLETE, COMPLETE. The arrivals remain blank. One carrier repeats a request for a replacement cup. Another asks whether the next watch has reported for duty. The third transmits only its berth number."},
		{"title":"THE BERTH WITHOUT A SHIP / 02","art":"archive","text":"The service cradle can repair the carriers remotely if the ship broadcasts their identifiers. That would strengthen their damaged shells before towing begins. It would also place their positions on the same network used by the hunters.\n\nCONTROL: We can keep them quiet, but we will be moving fragile archives across an open yard.\nSHIP: And if we call for help?\nCONTROL: The station will answer. Not every answer will be friendly.\n\nSUBSTRATE: I CAN HEAR THREE.\nSHIP: Three people?\nSUBSTRATE: THREE CONTINUATIONS. I DO NOT KNOW IF THAT IS THE SAME THING.\n\nThe ship resists the urge to put a comforting name on the icons. For now, they are three things that can still be lost."},
		{"title":"THE BERTH WITHOUT A SHIP / 03","art":"signal","text":"Control gives the retrieval order, then stops halfway through it.\n\nCONTROL: You are closer to the yard than I am. Choose.\n\nA broadcast will make each carrier tougher. Each delivery may draw an additional interceptor, though the hunters can only coordinate six active attackers at once. Silence leaves the original shells intact and draws the smaller response. Neither option makes the central cradle expendable.\n\nSHIP: When they reach the cradle, what happens to them?\nSUBSTRATE: THEY WILL NO LONGER HAVE TO ANSWER ALONE.\n\nThat is not a guarantee. It is enough to decide what the ship will try to do. Outside the glass, three berth lights wait for a tug that has not been built for this work."},
	]

static func choices(scene: String) -> Array[Dictionary]:
	if scene=="departure_room":
		return [{"id":"linked","label":"LINK THE THREE CHANNELS","effect":"Transport gains 60 hull; checkpoint details may contain four hunters instead of three (eight-alive cap)."},
			{"id":"independent","label":"KEEP THEIR CHANNELS SEPARATE","effect":"Standard transport hull/details; restore up to 15 ship hull before departure."}]
	return _early_choices(scene)

static func _early_choices(scene: String) -> Array[Dictionary]:
	if scene=="listening_room":
		return [{"id":"spoof","label":"SYNTHESIZE THE SIGNATURE","effect":"Spend 15 hull; face four gate escorts instead of eight."},
			{"id":"challenge","label":"ANNOUNCE THE APPROACH","effect":"Restore up to 15 hull; face the full eight gate escorts."}]
	return [{"id":"broadcast","label":"BROADCAST FOR REPAIR","effect":"Each carrier gains 50 maximum/current hull. Each delivery may summon up to three interceptors (six-alive cap)."},
		{"id":"silent","label":"KEEP THE CARRIERS QUIET","effect":"Original carrier hull; up to two interceptors per delivery (six-alive cap)."}]
